    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive output today rests on the shoulders of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries an elite 70.14 score into his matchup against Legumina. With a favorable SP xERA of 4.32 and a +8% efficiency boost from his prime spot in the two-hole, he is our clear priority play. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top-tier interest at 59.85; his lead-off role against Hart provides a significant +10% order bonus, offsetting the neutral platoon disadvantage. While **Brayan Rocchio** (46.89) and **Dominic Smith** (40.47) provide marginal value, their participation is required today to balance our caps, despite **Dominic Smith** facing a suboptimal left-on-left situation that suppressed his score.\n\nStrategy-wise, we are navigating a quiet day for our core assets. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Andy Pages** all sidelined by team off-days, our bench depth is essentially non-existent. **Drake Baldwin** is our most interesting decision; he hovered near the 60-point threshold, narrowly missing \"Strong\" status. Had his BvP metrics been slightly more aggressive, he might have pushed into the 65+ range, but we are satisfied with the exposure given the lack of alternatives among **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, or **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** today. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup for **Dominic Smith**. As a marginal start, his value is predicated on his presence in the batting order; should his status shift to \"Lineup Pending\" or a pinch-hit role, we risk burning a cap without production. There are no severe weather warnings currently impacting our active starters, but given the scarcity of stolen bases in our broader roster construction, we are monitoring **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** for potential late-game pinch-running opportunities if the game states for **Brayan Rocchio** or **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** trend toward a blowout. Proceed with the current active set, but keep **Hel